  VectorArrows: ['A vector has a direction and a length. Adding vectors chains their arrows, and scaling stretches one along its line.', 'Drag $u$ and $v$ so the sum points where you want. Try a negative scale.'],
  WeightedAverage: ['A weighted average always lies between its parts. Which part it is near depends only on the weights.', 'Drag the mix to each end, read the overall rate, and then change a group’s rate.'],
  ExpLog: ['$b^x$ grows by multiplying. Its inverse, the logarithm, asks which power gives a number.', 'Drag $x$ and note that the point and its mirror swap coordinates. Change the base and see the curves bend.'],
