  BisectorBoundary: ['Points equally far from two centroids form a straight line, the perpendicular bisector. Expanding the squares cancels the $\\|x\\|^2$ term, which is what makes it linear.', 'Drag each centroid and watch the line stay halfway between them. Compare the printed equation with the formula.'],
