  PlusPlusDrill: ['K-means++ draws the next centroid with probability proportional to $D$, the squared distance to the nearest centroid chosen so far.', 'List $D$ for every point, add them up, and divide the target’s $D$ by that sum.'],
  PlusPlusLab: ['The probability of a group is the sum over its points, so many moderately far points can outweigh one very far point.', 'Raise the distance of the lone point, then raise the group size. Find where the lone point stops being the likeliest pick.'],
  CalinskiDrill: ['$B$ tends to grow and $W$ to fall as $K$ rises, even with no structure. Dividing each by its degrees of freedom removes that automatic trend.', 'Compute each ratio separately, then divide the first by the second.'],
  KScores: ['Within-cluster spread, Calinski-Harabasz, silhouette and the gap statistic are all attempts to choose $K$, and each uses a different comparison.', 'Move $K$ and read each panel. Then switch to uniform noise and notice that every score still prefers some $K$.'],
